sections.in_scope:
This funds a coordinator that runs embargoed fixes for bugs in shared code, with downstream teams enrolled before the next bug. The mechanics are the bidder's. It must be able to:

- find who runs the vulnerable code (forks, deployments, chains, node operators);
- warn them privately;
- stage fixes and release them together;
- push operators to update after release.

Bids proposing a fixed patch day must show how it avoids telling attackers when to look. Bugs can come from any source; bids say where theirs will come from. The coordinator may pass researcher payment to a broker.
